\section{Data and Experimental Protocol}
The dataset contains {{ nsamples }} rows after removing rows with missing
target values; {{ nfeaturesused }} usable predictor columns were retained.
Preprocessing is embedded in each pipeline: median/most-frequent imputation
inside a \texttt{ColumnTransformer}, one-hot encoding with rare-level grouping
(\texttt{min\_frequency}=0.01) for categoricals, and optional standardization.

Model comparison uses {{ cvmode }} cross-validation: outer folds estimate
generalization performance, while inner folds tune hyperparameters via Optuna
(TPE sampler)~\citep{akiba2019optuna}. All folds share identical row
partitions across targets so predictions remain comparable. Reported metrics
aggregate out-of-fold test scores as mean $\pm$ standard deviation across
folds; the primary metric is \texttt{ {{ primarymetric }} }.

Algorithms compared: {{ algorithmlist }}. Core estimators:
\citep{pedregosa2011scikit}; gradient boosting:
\citep{chen2016xgboost,ke2017lightgbm}. Model inspection:
\citep{lundberg2017shap}. Supporting libraries:
\citep{harris2020array,mckinney2010data,hunter2007matplotlib,waskom2021seaborn}.

